{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453/events","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/pull/3453","id":5138905227,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBrVDM87-c85l","number":3453,"title":"[CuTe DSL] Preserve runtime tensor strides in Blackwell FMHA","user":{"login":"OutWhite","id":81479886,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNDc5ODg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81479886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite","html_url":"https://github.com/OutWhite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OutWhite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3687994693,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBrVDM87b0lVF","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/labels/inactive-30d","name":"inactive-30d","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-13T07:25:21Z","updated_at":"2026-09-20T09:14:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/pulls/3453","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/pull/3453","diff_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/pull/3453.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass/pull/3453.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nBlackwell CuTe DSL FMHA accepts dynamic-layout Q/K/V/O/LSE tensors, but rebuilt its internal layouts from problem sizes using packed strides. Because the original iterators were paired with these synthesized layouts, padded tensor views could be addressed as if they were contiguous and silently produce incorrect results.\n\nThis change:\n\n- maps the internal Q/K/V/O/LSE layouts from each input tensor runtime stride;\n- preserves the intentional zero batch stride for varlen inputs, whose batch offsets come from cumulative sequence lengths; and\n- corrects the LSE shape comment to match the actual allocation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Python syntax check for fmha.py.\n- NVIDIA GB200, CUDA 13.3, nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.7.0: contiguous FP16 FMHA compilation and reference check passed.\n- NVIDIA GB200: a local padded-stride case with B=2, GQA (8 query heads / 2 KV heads), and LSE enabled compiled and passed the reference check.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/3453/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}